ab.seg:
[p. 288]It is, indeed, worthy of remark that all our great poets
            have been good prose writers, as Chaucer, Spenser, Milton;
            and this probably rose from their just sense of metre.Note in Spurgeon: [The remarks on Chaucer's prose are reported at greater length in the Tatler, vol. ii, no. 224, May 23, 1831, p. 893.]
